BEITLAB DASHBOARD

Start the dashboard on the LCD:
    systemctl start beitlab-dashboard

Stop it and return to the LCD login:
    systemctl stop beitlab-dashboard

Make it the default LCD interface at boot:
    systemctl enable beitlab-dashboard

Return to on-demand operation:
    systemctl disable beitlab-dashboard

Starting pingpong or Doom stops the dashboard while the game owns the
framebuffer. `game stop`, a normal game exit, or a game crash returns to the
dashboard automatically.

The clock is NTP-synced by systemd-timesyncd. The dashboard then asks an
IP geolocation service for city, region, country and timezone, writes
/etc/localtime and shows that location under the clock.

Collect and print one sample without opening the framebuffer:
    beitlab-dashboard --once
